<title>USA: Durham, N.C., sets school building plan.</title>
<headline>Durham, N.C., sets school building plan.</headline>
<dateline>DURHAM, N.C. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's Durham County School System has approved a spending plan for the $22.4 million it will receive from a state school bond issue, the News &amp; Observer reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The plan, approved 6-1 at a Tuesday school board meeting, calls for construction of a new elementary school, expansion at Brogdan Middle School, and renovations and repairs at 12 existing schools.</p>
<p>Durham will get $22.4 million in proceeds from the statewide $1.8 billion general obligation bond issue that voters approved in November for school construction.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
